7:* When a `srcset` attribute is allowed through a `Safelist` (e.g. `Safelist.relaxed().addAttributes("img", "srcset")`), the `Cleaner` now validates the attribute candidate by candidate: the value is split per the HTML `srcset` parsing rules (so commas inside `data:` URLs and quoted content are not mistaken for separators), a matching `'` or `"` pair wrapping an address delimits it (commas, whitespace, character references, and parentheses inside are part of the address) but the delimiting quotes are never carried into the output, and each candidate URL is checked against the same protocol policy as an ordinary `src` URL. A width descriptor is accepted only as a single strictly positive decimal integer with a lower-case `w` (zero, signs, fractions, duplicate or mixed descriptors, and overflow invalidate the candidate), and density descriptors accept a single finite strictly positive number; each malformed candidate is dropped on its own. Candidates whose decoded address cannot be written without quotes and still reparse as the same single candidate are dropped rather than quoted. If no candidate survives, the attribute is removed rather than left empty.
8:* The candidate-by-candidate `srcset` cleaning now also covers `<source>` elements inside a responsive `<picture>`, e.g. `Safelist.relaxed().addTags("picture", "source").addAttributes("img", "srcset").addAttributes("source", "srcset", "media", "type")`. A `source` `srcset` without a protocol policy of its own is checked against the same policy as the fallback `img` (its `srcset` policy, then its `src` policy), so identical candidate strings on a `source` and on the `img` are filtered and serialized verbatim identically; an explicit `source` protocol policy still takes precedence. Every `source`, fallback `img`, and nested `picture` is handled independently: a malformed candidate, unterminated quote, or fully invalid value removes only that element's `srcset` attribute, never the element, its other allowed attributes (`media`, `type`), its children, or sibling order, and it never interrupts cleaning of the other images. Whitelist gating is unchanged: when the `source` tag is not allowed the element does not appear in the output, and when `source` is allowed but `srcset` is not, only the attribute is removed.
51:* Improved source tracking for adopted formatting elements and malformed markup ending at EOF. [#2582](https://github.com/jhy/jsoup/pull/2582)
56:* Reduced retained memory when parsing with source position tracking enabled (`Parser#setTrackPosition(true)`). Source ranges are now stored in compact parser-owned span records instead of node and attribute user data, and `Position` objects are created lazily when source ranges are read. This cuts tracked DOM retained size by about 50-60% on representative benchmark documents, while keeping `Node#sourceRange()`, `Element#endSourceRange()`, and `Attribute#sourceRange()` behavior intact. [#2498](https://github.com/jhy/jsoup/pull/2498)
75:* Cleaned up the Maven build for the multi-release JAR so Java 8 and Java 11+ sources compile as separate source sets. This avoids spurious Java 8 compiler warnings from newer-language overlay sources, keeps long-running parser checks behind an explicit profile, and preserves the same published artifacts and runtime behavior.
83:* Updated the default HTML `TagSet` for current HTML elements: added `dialog`, `search`, `picture`, and `slot`; made `ins`, `del`, `button`, `audio`, `video`, and `canvas` inline by default (`Tag#isInline()`, aligned to phrasing content in the spec); and added readable `Element.text()` boundaries for controls and embedded objects via the new `Tag.TextBoundary` option. This improves pretty-printing and keeps normalized text from running adjacent words together. [#2493](https://github.com/jhy/jsoup/pull/2493)
90:* `Cleaner` no longer duplicates enforced attributes when the input `Document` preserves attribute case. A case-variant source attribute is now replaced by the enforced attribute in the cleaned output. [#2476](https://github.com/jhy/jsoup/issues/2476)
186:* When cloning an Element, the clone would retain the source's cached child Element list (if any), which could lead to incorrect results when modifying the clone's child elements. [#2334](https://github.com/jhy/jsoup/issues/2334)
352:  root `Document` node. This enables source position tracking on the Document node (which was previously unset). And
361:* When tracking source ranges, a text node following an invalid self-closing element may be left
